# Git worktrees
.worktrees/
.claude/worktrees/

# User-specific Claude settings — glob covers .pre-prune-* backups per
# Vanta 2026-07-26 security audit (find-b82d7f1f9e88 / Aletheia F91):
# .claude/settings.local.json.pre-prune-2026-07-23 slipped past exact match.
.claude/settings.local.json*

# 2026-05-11 audit-transparency pass (Aether + Andrew, addressing
# Grok's Schneier finding on gitignored-folders-escaping-audit):
# on the EXPERIMENTAL repo, agent definitions are part of the lived
# substrate that audit-vantage needs read access to. The main
# DivineOS template keeps these ignored (clean-slate for fresh
# clones). Here, .claude/agents/ is tracked. Agent-memory runtime
# state stays ignored because it's noisy and regenerable.
.claude/agent-memory/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
# Anchored to the repo root (2026-08-18). These come from the stock Python
# template, where they name build artefacts that only ever appear at the top
# level. Unanchored, `lib/` matches a directory called lib at ANY depth — and
# it silently swallowed `.claude/hooks/lib/`, so the shared remedy allowlist
# that keeps sixteen gates' exits open lived on one machine's disk and was
# never in the repo at all. A fresh clone would have had sixteen gates
# sourcing a file that does not exist, failing quietly back to the deadlock
# the file was written to end. Found by a test that could not see the library
# it was testing.
/lib/
/lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

