/family/*_ledger.db-wal

# Canonical-substrate marker — opt-in flag the operator places at the
# parent repo root to indicate "this is a continuous Aether substrate;
# worktrees should share my event ledger." When absent (default for
# fresh template clones), each worktree gets its own ledger — correct
# for new agents bootstrapping continuity. When present, worktree
# sessions inherit the parent's accumulated history. Resolution logic
# in core/_ledger_base.py:_get_db_path. Andrew's workspace has it;
# the published template does not.
/.divineos_canonical
# Data-home marker: points ledger + knowledge + all substrate outside the
# repo entirely, so branch checkout cannot swap the DB. Andrew 2026-07-05
# night caught that my working ledger had been reset to 1.2k events on
# 2026-07-02 while a 31k pre-reset snapshot lived elsewhere on the machine.
# Root cause: DB inside the repo tree at src/data/event_ledger.db, and a
# past commit (c3b2df0a) had at some point unignored databases, so a branch
# containing a tracked DB would restore its snapshot on checkout and
# overwrite the accumulating local ledger. Fix: marker file points at
# ~/.divineos/, DB lives outside every worktree, git can never touch it.
# Marker itself MUST stay gitignored or the same shape recurs one layer up.
/.divineos_data_home

